Z||000029||Mach10||08-12-2001||05:15 PM||||Oh, snapped exhaust studs?!? SHITTY.<BR>You can drill'em but it's a pain. Bad angle. I've not done it before. Should be some more help on the forum. Do you have anything left to grab onto? If so, I'd suggest welding a rod onto it like a T and whack it with a hammer, after letting it float in WD-40 for a while. They are studs, so if you get the rest of them out, pull the manifold off, and work from there. I'm pretty sure that the studs are threaded in. Just hope they're not rusted in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> Otherwise, I can recommend a mechanic who should be able to do it. Cost you nothing for parts, but labour is a biotch. ||||reg||7
